{"id":"mahabharata-3-107","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":107,"title":"सप्ताधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 107 · Bhagiratha's austerities","summary":{"en":"Dilipa's son Bhagiratha, grieved to learn that his ancestors lie unpurified, goes to the Himalaya and practises austerities for a thousand years. Ganga appears and agrees to descend, but says that only Shiva can bear the force of her fall.","kn":"ಪಿತೃಗಳು ಪಾವನರಾಗದೆ ಬಿದ್ದಿದ್ದಾರೆಂದು ತಿಳಿದು ದುಃಖಿತನಾದ ದಿಲೀಪನ ಮಗ ಭಗೀರಥನು ಹಿಮಾಲಯಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗಿ ಸಾವಿರ ವರ್ಷ ತಪಸ್ಸು ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಗಂಗೆ ಪ್ರತ್ಯಕ್ಷಳಾಗಿ ಇಳಿಯಲು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಆದರೆ ತನ್ನ ಪತನದ ವೇಗವನ್ನು ಶಿವನೊಬ್ಬನೇ ತಡೆಯಬಲ್ಲನು ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"दिलीप के पुत्र भगीरथ यह जानकर दुःखी होते हैं कि उनके पूर्वज अपवित्र पड़े हैं, और हिमालय जाकर हज़ार वर्ष तप करते हैं। गंगा प्रकट होकर उतरने को सहमत होती हैं, पर कहती हैं कि उनके गिरने का वेग केवल शिव ही सह सकते हैं।","te":"పితరులు పావనం కాకుండా పడి ఉన్నారని తెలిసి దుఃఖించిన దిలీపుని కుమారుడు భగీరథుడు హిమాలయాలకు వెళ్లి వెయ్యేళ్లు తపస్సు చేస్తాడు. గంగ ప్రత్యక్షమై దిగడానికి అంగీకరిస్తుంది, కానీ తన పతన వేగాన్ని శివుడొక్కడే భరించగలడంటుంది.","ta":"முன்னோர்கள் தூய்மையடையாமல் கிடக்கிறார்கள் என்று அறிந்து வருந்திய திலீபனின் மகன் பகீரதன் இமயம் சென்று ஆயிரம் ஆண்டுகள் தவம் செய்கிறான். கங்கை தோன்றி இறங்க இசைகிறாள், ஆனால் தன் வீழ்ச்சியின் வேகத்தை ஶிவன் ஒருவரே தாங்க முடியும் என்கிறாள்.","ml":"ദിലീപന്റെ പുത്രനായ ഭഗീരഥൻ, പൂർവ്വികർ ശുദ്ധീകരിക്കപ്പെടാതെ കിടക്കുന്നുവെന്നറിഞ്ഞ് ദുഃഖിച്ച്, ഹിമാലയത്തിൽ ആയിരം വർഷം തപസ്സ് ചെയ്യുന്നു. ഗംഗ പ്രത്യക്ഷയായി ഇറങ്ങാൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു, പക്ഷേ അവളുടെ പതനത്തിന്റെ ശക്തി താങ്ങാൻ ശിവന് മാത്രമേ കഴിയൂ എന്ന് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.107; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स तु राजा महेष्वासश्चक्रवर्ती महारथः ।\nबभूव सर्वलोकस्य मनोनयननन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king, a great archer and great charioteer, a universal emperor, became a delight to the minds and eyes of the whole world."}},{"n":2,"text":"स शुश्राव महाबाहुः कपिलेन महात्मना ।\nपितॄणां निधनं घोरमप्राप्तिं त्रिदिवस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty-armed one heard from the great Kapila of his forefathers' dreadful death and of their failure to reach heaven."}},{"n":3,"text":"स राज्यं सचिवे न्यस्य हृदयेन विदूयता ।\nजगाम हिमवत्पार्श्वं तपस्तप्तुं नरेश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving the kingdom with his minister, his heart pained, the lord of men went to the side of the Himalaya to practise austerity."}},{"n":4,"text":"आरिराधयिषुर्गङ्गां तपसा दग्धकिल्बिषः ।\nसोऽपश्यत नरश्रेष्ठ हिमवन्तं नगोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing to please the Ganga by austerity, his sins burned away, best of men, he saw the Himalaya, best of mountains."}},{"n":5,"text":"शृङ्गैर्बहुविधाकारैर्धातुमद्भिरलंकृतम् ।\nपवनालम्बिभिर्मेघैः परिष्वक्तं समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was adorned with peaks of many shapes rich in minerals and embraced on every side by clouds that hung on the wind."}},{"n":6,"text":"नदीकुञ्जनितम्बैश्च सोदकैरुपशोभितम् ।\nगुहाकन्दरसंलीनैः सिंहव्याघ्रैर्निषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was beautiful with river-groves, ridges and streams, and frequented by lions and tigers hiding in caves and hollows."}},{"n":7,"text":"शकुनैश्च विचित्राङ्गैः कूजद्भिर्विविधा गिरः ।\nभृङ्गराजैस्तथा हंसैर्दात्यूहैर्जलकुक्कुटैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was filled with birds of varied colours calling in many tongues, bhringarajas, swans, datyuhas and water-cocks,"}},{"n":8,"text":"मयूरैः शतपत्रैश्च कोकिलैर्जीवजीवकैः ।\nचकोरैरसितापाङ्गैस्तथा पुत्रप्रियैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"peacocks, shatapatras, cuckoos, jivanjivakas, chakoras, those with dark eye corners, and putrapriyas."}},{"n":9,"text":"जलस्थानेषु रम्येषु पद्मिनीभिश्च संकुलम् ।\nसारसानां च मधुरैर्व्याहृतैः समलंकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was crowded in its lovely pools with lotus beds and decorated with the sweet calls of cranes."}},{"n":10,"text":"किंनरैरप्सरोभिश्च निषेवितशिलातलम् ।\nदिशागजविषाणाग्रैः समन्ताद्घृष्टपादपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its rock faces were frequented by kinnaras and apsaras, and trees were rubbed all round by the tusk tips of the elephants of the quarters."}},{"n":11,"text":"विद्याधरानुचरितं नानारत्नसमाकुलम् ।\nविषोल्बणैर्भुजंगैश्च दीप्तजिह्वैर्निषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vidyadharas roamed there, it was full of many jewels, and fierce poisonous serpents with flaming tongues lived there."}},{"n":12,"text":"क्वचित्कनकसंकाशं क्वचिद्रजतसंनिभम् ।\nक्वचिदञ्जनपुञ्जाभं हिमवन्तमुपागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In places it looked like gold, in others like silver, in others like heaps of collyrium; such was the Himalaya he came to."}},{"n":13,"text":"स तु तत्र नरश्रेष्ठस्तपो घोरं समाश्रितः ।\nफलमूलाम्बुभक्षोऽभूत्सहस्रं परिवत्सरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There that best of men took up fierce austerity, living on fruit, roots and water for a thousand years."}},{"n":14,"text":"संवत्सरसहस्रे तु गते दिव्ये महानदी ।\nदर्शयामास तं गङ्गा तदा मूर्तिमती स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a thousand divine years had passed, the great river Ganga herself appeared to him in bodily form."}},{"text":"गङ्गोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ganga said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"किमिच्छसि महाराज मत्तः किं च ददानि ते ।\nतद्ब्रवीहि नरश्रेष्ठ करिष्यामि वचस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, what do you want from me, and what shall I give you? Tell me, best of men, and I will do what you say."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमुक्तः प्रत्युवाच राजा हैमवतीं तदा ।\nपितामहा मे वरदे कपिलेन महानदि ।\nअन्वेषमाणास्तुरगं नीता वैवस्वतक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the king replied to the daughter of the Himalaya: \"Giver of boons, great river, my forefathers were taken by Kapila to Yama's abode while searching for the horse."}},{"n":17,"text":"षष्टिस्तानि सहस्राणि सागराणां महात्मनाम् ।\nकापिलं तेज आसाद्य क्षणेन निधनं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Sixty thousand great Sagaras met death in an instant, touched by Kapila's fire."}},{"n":18,"text":"तेषामेवं विनष्टानां स्वर्गे वासो न विद्यते ।\nयावत्तानि शरीराणि त्वं जलैर्नाभिषिञ्चसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Though they perished so, they cannot dwell in heaven as long as you do not sprinkle those bodies with your waters."}},{"n":19,"text":"स्वर्गं नय महाभागे मत्पितॄन्सगरात्मजान् ।\nतेषामर्थेऽभियाचामि त्वामहं वै महानदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Great and fortunate one, lead my forefathers, the Sagaras, to heaven. For them, great river, I beg you.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा वचो राज्ञो गङ्गा लोकनमस्कृता ।\nभगीरथमिदं वाक्यं सुप्रीता समभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the king's words, Ganga, honoured by the worlds, was pleased and said this to Bhagiratha:"}},{"n":21,"text":"करिष्यामि महाराज वचस्ते नात्र संशयः ।\nवेगं तु मम दुर्धार्यं पतन्त्या गगनाच्च्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Great king, I will do as you say, without doubt. But my force when I fall from the sky is hard to bear."}},{"n":22,"text":"न शक्तस्त्रिषु लोकेषु कश्चिद्धारयितुं नृप ।\nअन्यत्र विबुधश्रेष्ठान्नीलकण्ठान्महेश्वरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the three worlds no one can hold it, king, except the best of the gods, the blue-throated Maheshvara."}},{"n":23,"text":"तं तोषय महाबाहो तपसा वरदं हरम् ।\nस तु मां प्रच्युतां देवः शिरसा धारयिष्यति ।\nकरिष्यति च ते कामं पितॄणां हितकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Mighty-armed one, please that boon-giver Hara by austerity. That god will hold me on his head when I fall, and will fulfil your wish for the good of your forefathers.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा वचो राजन्महाराजो भगीरथः ।\nकैलासं पर्वतं गत्वा तोषयामास शंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words, king, the great king Bhagiratha went to Mount Kailasa and pleased Shankara."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततस्तेन समागम्य कालयोगेन केनचित् ।\nअगृह्णाच्च वरं तस्माद्गङ्गाया धारणं नृप ।\nस्वर्गवासं समुद्दिश्य पितॄणां स नरोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting him after some time, that best of men, king, received from him the boon of holding the Ganga, for the sake of his forefathers' dwelling in heaven."}}]}]}